# Auto versioning script
[![MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green)](https://github.com/virtualmode/version.py/blob/main/LICENSE)

.NET implementation
===================

Run:

```bash
# Run a file-based app.
dotnet [run] Version.cs [-- options]
# On Unix you can execute file-based apps directly using just the source file name.
./Version.cs [options]
# If the shebang in the Version.cs doesn't work, try:
#!/usr/bin/env dotnet
#!/usr/local/share/dotnet/dotnet --
```

Pipe code from stdin:

```bash
echo 'Console.WriteLine("Echo from stdin!");' | dotnet run -
```

Build:

```bash
# Compile your file-based app.
dotnet build Version.cs
# Manual restore.
dotnet restore Version.cs
dotnet build --no-restore Version.cs
dotnet run --no-build Version.cs
```

Clean:

```bash
# Remove build artifacts.
dotnet clean Version.cs
# Delete cache for file-based apps in a directory.
dotnet clean file-based-apps
```

Publish:

```bash
dotnet publish Version.cs -o bin
```

Package as tool:

```bash
dotnet pack Version.cs
```
